  "details": "- Rebase onto the Oracle unbound-1.6.6-5.0.3.el7_8 source RPM\n- The TuxCare duplicate of the ds_create_dnskey_digest() buffer-length check in\n  validator/val_sigcrypt.c is dropped; the vendor's 1001-orabug40081199 patch\n  carries the same fix and is applied together with its 1002-orabug40081199\n  regression test\n- The vendor's two Orabug 37387426 DNSSEC backports (the validation-complexity\n  cap in validator/val_sigcrypt.c and the NSEC3 closest-encloser iteration cap\n  in validator/val_nsec3.c) ship in the source RPM but are not declared or\n  applied; the existing TuxCare backports of the same two upstream commits are\n  kept instead, because the later TuxCare validator work is written against\n  their dnskeyset_verify_rrset_sig() and nsec3_prove_nods() signatures and does\n  not apply on top of the Oracle variants",
